the 1987 Regulations means the Police Pensions Regulations 1987

S.I. 1987/257.
									, and “the 1987 scheme” means the pension scheme established by those Regulations;

the 2006 Regulations means the Police Pensions Regulations 2006

S.I. 2006/3415.
									, and “the 2006 scheme” means the pension scheme established by those Regulations;

the 2015 Regulations means the Police Pensions Regulations 2015

S.I. 2015/445.
									;

the PSP Directions 2022 means the Public Service Pensions (Exercise of Powers, Compensation and Information) Directions 2022

Published on 15 December 2022 and accessible online at https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/public-service-pensions-and-judicial-offices-act-2022-treasury-directions. A hard copy is available on written request to His Majesty’s Treasury, 1 Horse Guards Road, London, SW1A 2HQ.
									;

is not a pensioner member

See section 109(3) of PSPJOA 2022 the meaning of “pensioner member”.
										 in relation to that service;

the legacy scheme, in relation to a member, means whichever of the 1987 scheme or the 2006 scheme is the relevant Chapter 1 legacy scheme

See section 4 of PSPJOA 2022 for the meaning of “the relevant Chapter 1 legacy scheme”.
									 for the member, and “legacy scheme benefits” means benefits calculated in accordance with that scheme;

the reformed scheme means the pension scheme established by the 2015 Regulations, and “reformed scheme benefits” means new scheme benefits

See section 34 of the PSPJOA 2022 for the meaning of “new scheme benefits”.
									 under the reformed scheme;

remediable police service means, in relation to a member, the member’s remediable service
See section 1 of the PSPJOA 2022 for the meaning of “remediable service”. in an employment or office that is pensionable service
See section 110(1) of PSPJOA 2022 for the meaning of “pensionable service”. under a police pension scheme;

cash equivalent means an amount calculated in accordance with regulations made under section 30 of WRPA 1999

In accordance with section 110(1) of PSPJOA 2022, “WRPA 1999” means the Welfare Reform and Pensions Act 1999 (c. 30).
											;

which are attributable (directly or indirectly) to a pension credit

See section 19(7) of PSPJOA 2022 for the meanings of “pension debit” and “pension credit”.
												;

a Chapter 1 scheme

See section 33 of PSPJOA 2022 for the meaning of “Chapter 1 scheme”.
											;

would be a payment described in regulation 6 of the Registered Pension Schemes (Authorised Payments) Regulations 2009

S.I. 2009/1171. Regulation 6 was amended by section 42(6)(a) of the Finance Act 2014 (c. 26).
											 (“the 2009 Regulations”) as if regulation 6(1)(a) of those Regulations were omitted, the compensatable amount is to be reduced by the amount equal to the income tax that would be chargeable on it as if regulation 3(b) of the 2009 Regulations applied to it;

an ill-health award under regulation B3

Regulation B3 was amended by SI 1990/805.
										 of the 1987 Regulations;
